Stacked footage plays faster and no longer runs out of memory in the browser: the three commits of our
upstream pull request https://github.com/storytold/effectcraft/pull/507 (branch perf/footage-playback of
daijro/effectcraft-fix), as one diff. This copy is backported to the newest release, v0.6.0 (pr-507.diff is the pull request itself, for the newest commit).
  1. The layer cache stays within 512 MB and the footage cache within 256 MB on wasm32: 8 stacked 1080p
     clips used to run the page out of memory after about 45 s.
  2. Below Full resolution, movie frames are downscaled in Y'CbCr before converting to RGBA
     (FootageSource::frame_at_size), instead of converting at full size and resampling.
  3. 8/16 bpc quantisation rounds with floor on wasm (same values, faster).
Verify: 1, 2, 4 and 8 stacked copies of a 1080p H.264 clip play at about 29/15/7.5/3.9 fps at Third
  resolution (24/12/6/3 without it), and 8 layers play for minutes without the page running out of memory.
If upstream changes: keep this the same change as the pull request, re-fitted to the code. Once upstream
  has merged the pull request (or does the same thing natively), empty this file: the build stops applying it.

